    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="1470" n="1454" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/10–1851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">GATT</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Delegation</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-18T17:41:00-05:00">October 18,
                            1951—5:41 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Gatt 104. House Banking and Currency Comite has scheduled hearings Oct 19 on
                    repeal Sec 104. Thorp and McCormick, Agric, will testify. Efforts continuing to
                    get Senate action. House hearings may help in getting Senate action.</p>
                <p>Congress, however, pushing for adjournment by night October 19. If Congress
                    adjourns, then, chances getting repeal Sec 104 practically nil. If it does not,
                    we still have fighting chance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
